<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Inverse of Polynomials — checking two functions are inverses by composition</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \( f(x) = {@fx@} \) and \( g(x) = {@gx@} \).</p>
<ol class="tb-parts">
  <li><p>Find \( f(g(x)) \) and simplify it.</p>
    <div>\( f(g(x)) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div></li>
  <li><p>Hence, is \(g\) the inverse of \(f\)?</p>
    <div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div></li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(g\) is the <strong>inverse</strong> of \(f\) exactly when composing them gives the identity, \(f(g(x)) = x\) for every \(x\). (For linear functions this one check is enough; in general \(g(f(x)) = x\) is also needed.)</p>
<ol class="tb-parts">
  <li><p>Substitute the whole expression \(g(x)\) for every \(x\) in \(f\):</p>
  \[ f(g(x)) = {@m@}\left({@gx@}\right) [[if test="is(b>0)"]]+ {@b@}[[else]]- {@-b@}[[/if]] = {@ta_composed@}. \]</li>
  <li><p>[[if test="is_identity"]]This simplifies to exactly \(x\), so \(g\) is the inverse of \(f\).[[else]]This does not simplify to \(x\), so \(g\) is not the inverse of \(f\), even though it looks similar. The inverse of \(f\) is \({@(x-b)/m@}\).[[/if]]</p></li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[m: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0,1,-1]);
b: rand_with_prohib(-9,9,[0]);
is_true_inverse: is(rand(2)=1);
fx: m*x + b;
/* the true inverse is (x-b)/m; the impostor has the wrong sign on b */
gx: if is_true_inverse then (x-b)/m else (x+b)/m;
ta_composed: ratsimp(m*gx + b);
is_identity: is(ratsimp(ta_composed - x) = 0);
/* Diagnostic: multiplied f and g instead of composing. A quadratic, so never equal to ta_composed. */
wrong_product: expand(fx*gx);
opts2: [["yes", is_identity, "Yes"], ["no", not is_identity, "No"]];
validate_x(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [x])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Write your answer in terms of x only.";]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
